# What the Vercel CLI uploads before it builds.
#
# The CLI composes a deployment from the REPOSITORY ROOT — the project's Root
# Directory (`frontend`) only decides where the build runs — so anything large
# in the tree is uploaded first and can abort the deployment outright:
#
#     Uploading [====================] (1.5GB/1.5GB)
#     Error: File size limit exceeded (100 MB)
#
# That 1.5 GB was the agent workspace (.freebuff, 750 MB), the Python backend
# (405 MB) and a demo video: none of it is needed to build the frontend, and
# none of it changes the build output. `node_modules` and `.git` are excluded by
# the CLI already; they are listed anyway so the intent is explicit and a future
# CLI change cannot silently start uploading them again.
#
# Keep this list to non-frontend and regenerated paths only — excluding
# something under frontend/ that the build actually reads would produce a
# deployment that serves a broken bundle.

.freebuff
backend
ML
uploads
.git
node_modules
dist
.vercel
.venv
.dockerignore
__pycache__
.pytest_cache

# Binary artifacts and logs that live in the tree but have no business in a
# deployment upload.
*.mp4
*.pkl
*.pdf
*.docx
*.log
